# Harness bootstrap (this repository only)

This checkout is the source of the governance harness, not a consumer of it. The
rules, hooks, and gates that should govern this session live in `claude/` and are
projected into `cursor/` by `translate/cursor.mjs`; `./sync.sh` installs `cursor/`
into `~/.cursor`, `claude/` into `~/.claude`, and `codex/` into `~/.codex`.

Claude Code sessions bootstrap themselves here: `.claude/settings.json` registers a
`SessionStart` hook that runs `claude/hooks/harness-sync.sh`, which compares the
live trees against this checkout and runs `./sync.sh` when they differ. Cursor has
no equivalent automatic entry point, so that step is yours to run.

## Do this first, before relying on any rule or gate

Run `./sync.sh` from the root of this checkout. It is idempotent, it never deletes
live files (a deliberate tradeoff after an earlier destructive incident), and it
stamps `~/.claude/.sync-source` so later sessions in other projects know where the
harness came from.

Until that runs, the rules loaded from `~/.cursor` are whatever was installed last,
which may predate every change in your working tree. The failure is silent: a stale
rule file reads exactly like a current one.

## Verifying rather than assuming

- `node translate/cursor.mjs --check` exits 0 when `cursor/` matches its `claude/`
  sources, 1 when a source edit has not been regenerated, and 2 on a source error.
  A nonzero exit means the payload itself is stale, and syncing would only install
  the staleness; run `node translate/cursor.mjs --write` first.
- `node translate/codex.mjs --check` does the same for the Codex payload.
- `diff -r cursor ~/.cursor` names the files that differ if you want the specific
  list rather than a verdict.

## What not to edit

Everything under `cursor/` is generated except `cursor/hooks/claude-hook-adapter.sh`,
`cursor/README.md`, and the two `cursor/commands/session-*.md` files, which the port
map classifies hand-authored. Editing any other file under `cursor/` is lost at the
next `--write`, and `--check` fails in CI and at push until it is reverted. Change
the `claude/` source or `translate/cursor-port-map.json` instead, then regenerate.
